    "items": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "In my bed at night",
          "I sought the one I love;",
          "I sought him, but did not find him. ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I will arise now and go about the city,",
          "through the streets and the plazas.",
          "I will seek the one I love.",
          "I sought him, but did not find him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The guards who go about the city found me.",
          "I asked them, “Have you seen the one I love? ”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I had just passed them",
          "when I found the one I love.",
          "I held on to him and would not let him go",
          "until I brought him to my mother’s house —",
          "to the chamber of the one who conceived me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Young women of Jerusalem, I charge you",
          "by the gazelles and the wild does of the field,",
          "do not stir up or awaken love",
          "until the appropriate time. ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Narrator"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who is this coming up from the wilderness",
          "like columns of smoke,",
          "scented with myrrh and frankincense",
          "from every fragrant powder of the merchant?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Look! Solomon’s bed",
          "surrounded by sixty warriors",
          "from the mighty men of Israel."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "All of them are skilled with swords",
          "and trained in warfare.",
          "Each has his sword at his side",
          "to guard against the terror of the night."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "King Solomon made a carriage for himself",
          "with wood from Lebanon."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He made its posts of silver,",
          "its back of gold,",
          "and its seat of purple.",
          "Its interior is inlaid with love",
          "by the young women of Jerusalem."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Go out, young women of Zion,",
          "and gaze at King Solomon,",
          "wearing the crown his mother placed on him",
          "on the day of his wedding —",
          "the day of his heart’s rejoicing."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
